<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna calleeprotostack: a store into the caller's home slot is dropped when its
    address is passed to a declared callee.

    MSVC x64 spills a value into the home slot its caller allocated above the
    return address and passes that slot by reference.  Qt emits it for every
    connect(sender, &Class::signal, ...): the member function pointer goes to
    entry rsp+0x18 and its address to QObject::connectImpl.

        140001000  48 83 ec 28            SUB   RSP,0x28
        140001004  48 8d 05 75 00 00 00   LEA   RAX,[worker_proc]
        14000100b  48 89 44 24 40         MOV   [RSP + 0x40],RAX   ; entry rsp+0x18
        140001010  48 8d 4c 24 40         LEA   RCX,[RSP + 0x40]
        140001015  e8 46 00 00 00         CALL  consume
        14000101a  48 83 c4 28            ADD   RSP,0x28
        14000101e  c3                     RET
        140001060  48 8b 01 c3            consume: MOV RAX,[RCX]; RET
        140001080  31 c0 c3               worker_proc: XOR EAX,EAX; RET

    calleeprotostack leaves a caller slot above a declared callee's frame
    unguarded unless the alias checker says a pointer can reach it, and the
    upstream checker only answers for locals below the return address.  The
    home slot's address escaped, so the call must keep its guard over it.

    Stage: P3 heritage call guarding, option calleeprotostack off|on.  Pass 1
    (off) guards every caller slot; pass 2 (on, the default) must keep the
    store as well.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x140001000">
4883ec28488d0575000000488944244048
8d4c2440e8460000004883c428c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x140001060">
488b01c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x140001080">
31c0c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x140001000" name="f"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x140001060" name="consume"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x140001080" name="worker_proc"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern void *consume(void **slot);</com>
  <com>option calleeprotostack off</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calleeprotostack on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPROTOSTACK HOMESLOT #1: both passes store worker_proc into the home slot" min="2" max="2">= worker_proc;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPROTOSTACK HOMESLOT #2: both passes pass the slot's address to consume" min="2" max="2">consume\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
